# Student Performance Prediction Using Decision Tree

## Aim

To predict whether a student will pass or fail using a Decision Tree Classifier.

## Objective

* Train a Decision Tree model on student data.
* Predict student results (Pass/Fail).
* Evaluate the model using accuracy and confusion matrix.

## Procedure

1. Import the required libraries.
2. Load the student performance dataset.
3. Split the dataset into training and testing data.
4. Train the Decision Tree Classifier.
5. Predict the test data.
6. Calculate accuracy and confusion matrix.
7. Visualize the decision tree and results.

## Result

The Decision Tree model was successfully implemented and tested on the student performance dataset. The model accurately predicted whether a student would pass or fail based on study hours, attendance, and assignments completed. The obtained accuracy and confusion matrix showed good classification performance.
